B.Vd=s(["Arunachal Pradesh is inhabited by 26 major tribes and over 100 sub-tribes.","Solung: Celebrated by the Adi tribe in 1st week of September after sowing seeds to seek a bountiful harvest.","Mopin: Galo festival in April; locals smear rice powder (Ette) on faces; Popir dance is performed.","Losar: Monpa Buddhist New Year marking start of spring in Tawang and West Kameng.","Boori Boot: Nyishi festival celebrated in February to welcome spring and prosperity.","Dree: Biggest festival of the Apatani tribe celebrated on 5th July in Ziro Valley; Daminda dance performed.","Nyethrii-Dow: Celebrated by the Hrusso (Aka) tribe in West Kameng in November.","Chalo-Loku: Harvest festival of the Nocte tribe in Tirap in October-November.","Longte Yullo: Oldest festival of the Nyishi tribe celebrated in April; notable for having NO animal sacrifice or ritual chanting.","Oriah: Main festival of the Wancho tribe in Longding held in March-April.","Reh: Celebrated on 1st February by the Idu Mishmi tribe; reverence to divine mother Nanyi Inyitaya.","Sangken: Buddhist water festival celebrated by Khamti and Singpho tribes on 14-16 April.","Si-Donyi: Celebrated by the Tagin tribe in January; reverence to Earth (Si) and Sun (Donyi).",'Nyokum-Yullo: Traditional agricultural festival of the Nyishi tribe celebrated on 26th February ("Nyok" = Earth, "Kum" = Togetherness).',"Tamladu: Ancient prayer festival of Digaru/Taraon Mishmi in Lohit on 15th February."],t.s)
